180: \nL181: More items\nL182: \nL183: # STAlloc\nL184: \nL185: ## Description\nL186: \nL187:   * STAlloc is a memory tool used to reduce memory fragmentation and improve memory utilization.\nL188:   * STAlloc actively leverages the predictable memory allocation pattern of large model training to perform ahead-of-time memory allocation planning.\nL189: \nL190: ## Compilation\nL191: \nL192:   * `cd Allocator && make`\nL193:   * See `Allocator/README.md` for more details\nL194: ## Env\nL195: Env  | Value  | Description\nL196: --- | --- | ---\nL197: `STALLOC_MODE`  | `[Torch (default), Trace, Alloc]`  | set the mode of STAlloc.\nL198: `STALLOC_LIB_PATH`  | path to STAlloc lib, required when using `STALLOC_MODE` is `Trace` or `Alloc`.  |\nL199: `STALLOC_MODEL_INFO_PATH`  | path to save model memory info, required when `STALLOC_MODE` is `Trace` or `Alloc`.  |\nL200: `STALLOC_DYNAMIC`  | `[0 (default), 1]`  | required in MoE model(without batchgemm) when `STALLOC_MODE` is `Trace` or `Alloc`.\nL201: `STALLOC_LOG_LEVEL`  | `[0, 1, 2, 3 (default)]`  | set the log level of STAlloc, the smaller the value, the more detailed the output content.\nL202: `STALLOC_STATIC_FALLBACK`  | `[0 (default), 1]`  | enable fallback in static-alloc, which will affect the performance\nL203: `STALLOC_TRACE_FAST_MODE`  | `[0 (default), 1]`  | use faster dynamic-allocator to trace, but this may lead to OOM, when the memory required by the model has reached the limit of GPU.\nL245: ### Step-1\nL246: \nL247:   * Set `export STALLOC_MODE=Torch` and run the training script.\nL248:   * Check if the GPU memory fragmentation of torch is severe.\nL249:     * Find this form of line in log : `dev0 : max_reserved:xx.xx, max_allocated:xx.xx, utilization:xx.xx%`\nL250:     * The smaller the `utilization`, the more severe of the fragmented storage.\nL253: ### Step-2\nL254: \nL255:   * Set `export STALLOC_MODE=Trace` and run the training script.\nL256: \nL257: ### Step-3\nL258: \nL259:   * Generate Plan. run the following command\nL260:   * `cd ${STALLOC_PATH}/Synthesizer`\nL261:   * `python main.py -model-memory-dir=XXXX`\nL262:   * exec `python mian.py --help` for more details\nL263: \nL264: ### Step-4\nL265: \nL266:   * Set `export STALLOC_MODE=Alloc` and run the training script.\nL267: \nL268: ## Others\nL269: \nL270: If you are using other version of Megatron-LM, you may need to check the path of patch functions, and modify in `utils/memory_patcher.py`.\nL271: ## License\nL272: \nL273: This project is licensed under the 【74†Apache License 2.0†www.apache.org】.\nL274: \nL275: ## About\nL276: \nL277: No description, website, or topics provided.\nL278: \nL279: ### Resources\nL280: \nL281: 【56†Readme】\nL282: \nL283: 【57†Apache-2.0 license】\nL284: \nL285: 【58†Activity】\nL286: \nL287: 【59†Custom properties】\nL288: \nL289: ### Stars\nL290: \nL291: 14 stars\nL292: \nL293: ### Watchers\nL294: \nL295: 0 watching\nL296: \nL297: ### Forks\nL298: \nL299: 【60†4 forks】\nL300: \nL301: 【61†Report repository】\nL302: \nL303: ## Releases\nL304: \nL305: ## Packages\nL306: \nL307: ## Contributors\nL308: \nL309: ## Languages\nL310: \nL311: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n"
